    "bookends": {
      "first": {
        "speaker": 0,
        "line": 2,
        "text": "I walked with a zombie. It does seem an odd thing to say. Had anyone said that to me a year ago, I'm not at all sure I would have known what a Zombie was. I might have had some notion -- that they were strange and frightening, and perhaps a little funny."
      },
      "last": {
        "speaker": 0,
        "line": 462,
        "text": "I wouldn't have minded waiting. I never mind waiting for you -- only we're dining with the Wilkins. I don't want it said all over Ottowa that the Hollands are always late."
      }
    },
